{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='draft/update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['rationale']=(\\\"The bounded-liveness consequence of the configuration loss is now witnessed. Receipt f5cb1459db5e418d9a9aa6987ef76dfc (exit 0, fourteen events, no parse loss) resolves both comparisons of the authority experiment: with RestoreCommittedLogs on, the restarted single-voter node was still a Follower after the whole 1500 ms sampling window and never became leader (witness event index 11), while the identical restart without the flag reached Leader inside the same window (evaluated event index 13). Together with the earlier witnesses, the account now runs from the lost configuration to an authority transition that never happens: the node's empty configuration routes runFollower into the 'no known peers' branch and keeps quorumSize() computed from that empty configuration, so the single-voter cluster stays without a leader indefinitely rather than for a bounded interval. The two other questions are unchanged and are not restated.\\\")\nd['sources']=[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":604,\\\"end_line\\\":620,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":724,\\\"end_line\\\":754,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_snapshot_config\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":655,\\\"end_line\\\":681,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"config_restore_committed_doc\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"config.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":242,\\\"end_line\\\":254,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_follower_election_abort\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":228,\\\"end_line\\\":246,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1087,\\\"end_line\\\":1094,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"log_commit_tracking_iface\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"log.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":194,\\\"end_line\\\":219,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"interface_statement\\\"}\n]\nd['knowledge']=[\n {\\\"ref\\\":\\\"@authority_behavior\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n  \\\"statement\\\":\\\"A node restarted with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs whose rebuilt configuration is empty stays a Follower and never campaigns: the latest configuration is empty, so runFollower takes the 'no known peers, aborting election' branch and quorumSize() returns one, while the same node restarted without the flag rebuilds the committed configuration and returns to Leader.\\\",\n  \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Single-voter configuration bootstrapped in the log, Config.RestoreCommittedLogs=true with CommitTrackingLogStore, no snapshot so the startup configuration scan starts above the committed configuration entry; observed over a 1500 ms window with a 50 ms election timeout.\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"raft_follower_election_abort\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"config_restore_committed_doc\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"f5cb1459db5e418d9a9aa6987ef76dfc\\\":[11,13]}}\n]\nd['interpretations']=[\n {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"ec0aa4e70fc945f59fb6d1ae7a1f1396-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"ec0aa4e70fc945f59fb6d1ae7a1f1396-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"raft_follower_election_abort\\\",\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"config_restore_committed_doc\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"f5cb1459db5e418d9a9aa6987ef76dfc\\\":[11,13]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Receipt f5cb1459db5e418d9a9aa6987ef76dfc (exit 0, fourteen events, no parse loss) settles both comparisons. Comparison 0 is violated by witness event index 11: after restarting the single-voter node with RestoreCommittedLogs on and no snapshot, became_leader is false and the final state is Follower across the whole 1500 ms sampling window, with after_latest_index 0 (admission event is the matching startup_before_restart with before_latest_index 1). Comparison 1 holds at evaluated event index 13: the identical restart without the flag reports became_leader true, final state Leader and after_latest_index 1, so the difference tracks the recovery flag and not restart timing. Source mechanism: with an empty latest configuration, runFollower's first branch logs 'no known peers, aborting election' and never sets Candidate (raft.go:228-232); even if it reached the candidate path, quorumSize() would be 1 while electSelf asks only the servers in the same empty configuration, so no vote is ever counted (raft.go:1087-1094); and the configuration is empty precisely because restoreFromCommittedLogs advanced lastApplied past the committed LogConfiguration before the startup scan (api.go:604-620 and 724-754). Consequence under the witnessed conditions: a single-voter cluster that restarts with this flag never regains a leader, so all client duties that require a leader stay pending indefinitely; the pending duty is not merely delayed but has no enabled path to completion, since the node's own committed log holds the configuration it would need. The same source branch applies to a node in a larger cluster, where it would remain unable to campaign and would also compute an empty quorum, but only the single-voter case is witnessed here.\\\",\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"ec0aa4e70fc945f59fb6d1ae7a1f1396-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"An empty rebuilt configuration keeps the node in the 'no known peers' follower branch, so it never campaigns while the flag-off control returns to Leader.\\\"}],\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The flag-off control reaches Leader inside the same 1500 ms window, so the non-campaigning is not a general restart delay.\\\",\\\"The library deliberately grants votes when the server list is empty (bootstrap affordance), which explains why such a node still answers vote requests; the witnessed defect is the state itself, not the vote-granting rule.\\\"],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"Only a single-voter configuration is exercised, so an election run under a stale multi-voter membership is not witnessed.\\\",\\\"The window is bounded at 1500 ms against a 50 ms election timeout, so a much later recovery is not excluded.\\\",\\\"The same experiment keeps no snapshot; the snapshot-age configuration variant is witnessed only through the configuration observation, not through this authority sample.\\\"]}\n]\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('patched ok')\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
