{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The bounded-liveness consequence is now witnessed. Receipt f5cb1459db5e418d9a9aa6987ef76dfc (exit 0, fourteen events) resolves both comparisons of the authority experiment: with RestoreCommittedLogs on, the restarted single-voter node stayed Follower for the entire 1500 ms window and never became leader (violated, witness event index 11, after_latest_index 0), while the identical restart without the flag reached Leader in the same window (control holds, evaluated index 13, after_latest_index 1). The interpretation for ec0aa4e70fc945f59fb6d1ae7a1f1396-question-0 is recorded as violated with defect_claim asserted, and a Behavior knowledge entry is promoted with that execution. The chain is now: restoreFromCommittedLogs advances lastApplied past the committed configuration, NewRaft's scan therefore never rebuilds it, runFollower's no-known-peers branch and an empty quorumSize keep the node from campaigning, so a single-voter cluster that restarts with this flag never regains a leader and client duties stay pending with no enabled path to completion. Counterevidence retained: the flag-off control isolates the recovery path, and the library's deliberate vote-granting on an empty configuration explains vote answers but not the lost state. The other two questions are unchanged.\"}"}}
